+Since wolf 0.2.31 it is made sooner. A program that can park, which is
+any program that calls `net_accept` or a net read or write, makes the
+runtime's readiness set and the thread that waits in it before `main`
+runs, so no park has to ask the host for a descriptor in the middle of
+serving. When the host has none to give, because the program was
+started at its descriptor limit, the program does not start. No line of
+`main` runs, standard error gets one line,
