+```
+
+and the exit status is 71, the number `sysexits(3)` gives an
+operating-system error. It is not a trap: nothing the program did is at
+fault, and a supervisor that reads 71 knows to look at the limit before
+it looks at the code. A program that cannot park makes no set at all,
+and neither the interpreter nor the checked machine has one to make.
 
